From d8ed3254fb31df9b720405f97554c4f25599d132 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: AERA | Erez Yaary <yaary@me.com>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 10:27:01 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] common/ui/filepick.c: the family's file dialog, several files
 at once

From EPlay's Add files (ui/addfiles.c and src/dirlist.c; Erez, 4 Nov
2026), as the hub asked (5 Nov 2026), for EPDF's EConvert and the next
app that takes several files: the AES's own objects with Selectric's
ways, the last ten folders, the type, the sort, a mask, sizes and dates,
a click, Shift-click, a drag, Control+A, All and None, the count and
bytes, folders taken whole, idle() every 20 ms while it is open.

What was EPlay's own is now the app's FP_SPEC: the title ("Add files"),
the default button ("Add"), the empty Folders line, the name of the
rigs' picture times on the console ("EPLAY picture add 110 ms") and the
Type pop-up's entries, a DL_TYPE table of names and extensions (12 at
most; with none, All files alone). The rest is EPlay's code as it was.

tests/dirlist: EPlay's checks of the folder (masks, the sorts with
folders first, the selection, sizes and dates, 5,000 entries) with its
types as a table, and the table's own (none, the first chosen, AIFC,
names without a dot): all pass, with AddressSanitizer.

tests/filepick: FPTEST.PRG opens it on a folder of music, a text file
and two folders with EPlay's types; run.py selects with Down and
Shift+Down, types a mask and clears it, takes all with Control+A and
adds them with Return; the files taken must be the five music files in
name order, idle() called, no CRASH.LOG. With --old it runs EPlay's own
(FPOLD.PRG, make old EPLAY=...) the same way and compares the five
screenshots pixel for pixel. On EmuTOS:

  Falcon:16     all passed, the five the same as EPlay's; opened in 110 ms
  Falcon-4:16   all passed, the five the same; 160 ms
  ST:mono       all passed, the five the same; 415 ms
  ST:med        all passed, the five the same; 420 ms

No pixel changed. Seen on ST:med (EPlay never runs there): with an
8-pixel font a folder's shape reaches into the row above it. That is
for a change of its own, with its pictures.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
